  Radio:
    Title: Radio log
    Normal: A tune ends. Two beats pass, then it starts again. Close to the grille I can hear the faint rasp of the speaker.
    Changed: The speaker shrieks. I turn it down, but the tune goes on. It is coming from the lake.
    Special: 
  WindVane:
    Title: Vane log
    Normal: Wind combs through the treetops. The blade turns with it.
    Changed: The wind catches my coat. Above me the blade does not move.
    Special: When the beam found the tracks, something creaked overhead. The blade had started turning again.
  Lake:
    Title: Shore log
    Normal: The seal at the bank holds. My reflection is the only thing I can see beneath the drifting snow.
    Changed: The cut at the bank is broken. The water is too dark to see what lies beneath.
    Special: My watch says sunrise has passed. The ridge is black. Only the middle of the lake gives off light.
  Day1Guide: Check the radio, the vane and the shore.
  Day2Guide: Follow the boot prints south to the cave.
  Day3Guide: Follow the deep prints inside the fence to the woods north of the cabin.
  Day3FoundGuide: The second tablet bears the fifth day's mark.
  Day4Guide: Take the south path to the old ritual stones near the cave.
  Day4FoundGuide: The third tablet bears the seventh day's mark.
  Day5Guide: Go through the gap by the vane. Follow the tune to the shore.
  Day5FoundGuide: The voice is still coming from the water.
  Day6Guide: Head north along the bank to the old listening post.
  Day6FoundGuide: Fit the missing stones to the listening tablet. Press Enter to set them.
  Day6ActiveGuide: Listen from behind the timber wall. Remember which bell rings.
  SolarRecord: 'Sunrise log


    Dawn should have broken an hour ago. The sun hangs black inside a white rim. The lake is bright enough to see from the cabin. The clock keeps good time.


    That rim is on the chest behind the cabin. Take another look at the bearing dial.'
  HandoverRecord: "Handover book \xB7 Eighth day\n\nRelief due this morning. No one at the gate. No message on the set. I have entered the time by the wall clock; the sky is no use to me now.\n\nCheck the ninth-day mark on the fourth tablet. Take the tool from Chest A and listen for the forest bells. The last stone is still out there. Wait indoors until nightfall, then search the bank."
  Day7Guide: Check the sunrise log beside the radio.
  Day7CipherGuide: Compare the radio, sun and vane with the dial. Open Chest A and take the tablet.
  Day7BeamGuide: Switch on the torch by the vane. Hold it on the moving tracks, then switch it off.
  Day7LockedGuide: The vane turns while the beam holds. Break the beam and watch the tracks.
  Day7ReadyGuide: The bells tell you where it is. The beam buys time.
  Day8Guide: Relief is due. Read the book by the cabin door.
  Day8ToolGuide: Still no relief. Check Chest A and the path to the lake.
  Day8ListeningGuide: The tool is yours. Mend the listening tablet at the north bank before nightfall.
  Day8ReadyGuide: After {hour}, search the shore. Bring the stone back to the cabin stand.
  FoundGuide: First tablet recorded. Retrace the trail to camp.
